def smallest_change(items):
    """
    Given a sequence items of values, determine how many entries might need to be altered
    to make the sequence read the same both ways. A palindromic sequence is one that
    is read the same backwards and forwards. A single modification can replace one entry with any other.

    The function returns the count of differing pairs between corresponding elements from start and end,
    summing one per mismatched pair. The middle element is ignored if the length is odd.

    For example:
    smallest_change([1,2,3,5,4,7,9,6]) == 4
    smallest_change([1, 2, 3, 4, 3, 2, 2]) == 1
    smallest_change([1, 2, 3, 2, 1]) == 0
    """
